<title>NETHERLANDS: Akzo Nobel takes over Polish paints plant.</title>
<headline>Akzo Nobel takes over Polish paints plant.</headline>
<dateline>ARNHEM, Netherlands 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch chemicals group Akzo Nobel NV said on Thursday that it bought Polish paints manufacturer Nobiles, Kujawska Paints and Lacquers Factory, based in Wloclawek.  </p>
<p>Nobiles will be brought into Akzo's Decorative Coatings (North) business unit, the Dutch group said in a statement, adding that the move further strengthened its position in the construction paints sector in central and eastern Europe.</p>
<p>Nobiles, Kujawska, one of the leading Polish construction paint makers, has annual sales of around 100 million guilders and employs 780 staff. The firm also makes industrial coatings, resins and car re-finishes.</p>
<p>No financial details were disclosed.</p>
